    "narrative": "Ghost Ride the WHIP enters today\u2019s slate with **Corbin Carroll** serving as our clear offensive anchor. With a commanding score of 87.13, **Corbin Carroll** is positioned perfectly to exploit the soft matchup against Tomoyuki Sugano; the favorable SP_xERA of 5.02 and a +6% dynamic platoon boost make him a high-ceiling candidate for stolen bases, a category we continue to prioritize. Close behind is **Tyler Soderstrom**, whose 76.90 rating is heavily influenced by a potent combination of a +10% park factor and the aforementioned matchup against the hittable Nick Martinez. **Gabriel Moreno** rounds out the elite tier at 71.10, benefiting from a high-leverage spot in the order and a favorable platoon advantage that makes him a premier asset at the catcher position for this evening.\n\nOur most difficult bench decision involved **Jose Caballero**, who finished just outside the starting threshold with a score of 43.67. While **Jose Caballero** offers valuable stolen base upside, the optimizer penalized his expected position in the bottom third of the lineup and a suboptimal platoon split against Bryan Woo. We ultimately prioritized the higher reliability of **Max Muncy** and **Henry Bolte**, both of whom project for stronger offensive environments. We continue to monitor the status of **James Wood**, who remains stashed on the IL, alongside depth pieces like **Vinnie Pasquantino**, **Giancarlo Stanton**, **Trevor Story**, **Dalton Rushing**, **Edwin Arroyo**, and **Travis Bazzana**.\n\nA note of caution: today\u2019s lineup remains fluid with several \"Lineup Pending\" designations. **Josh Naylor** and **Cole Young** face a tougher-than-average test against Ryan Weathers (3.41 xERA), and while they maintain starting status, their sub-50 scores underscore the risk. Furthermore, **Austin Riley** continues to struggle to clear our internal thresholds, yielding a marginal 47.46 score as he navigates a matchup against Nolan McLean. All starters should be treated as high-priority, though managers must remain vigilant for any late-breaking lineup shifts that could invalidate these base projections.",
